When unlocked, these Rooms appear attached to a Main Path Boss Room once the [[Boss]] is defeated (or appear at the end of Alternate Path [[Chapter]]). These Rooms contain an entrance to the Alternate Path Floors. These Rooms have different requirements to open them, based on the [[Chapter]] they are barring entrance to:

# In floors 1-2, the door requires a key to unlock the entrance to {{s|Downpour}} or {{s|Dross}}.
# In floors 3-4, the door requires two bombs to unlock the entrance to {{s|Mines}} or {{s|Ashpit}}.
# In floors 5-6, the door requires sacrificing two hearts to unlock the entrance to {{s|Mausoleum}} or {{s|Gehenna}} (except on {{s|Depths}} II and its variants, where this door doesn't appear).{{dlc-}}

==== {{a|A Strange Door}} Exit Room ====
[[File:A_Strange_Door_locked.png|98px]]

When unlocked, this room appears above the starting room of the second floor of Chapter 3, containing a trapdoor leading to a special version of the second floor of Chapter 3.5. This door is generally opened by obtaining and sacrificing either {{i|The Polaroid}} or the {{i|The Negative}}. The door can also be opened with {{t|Broken Padlock}}, {{i|Cracked Orb}}, {{t|Faded Polaroid}}, {{p|Soul of Cain}}, or {{i|Sharp Key}}.

=== {{dlc|a+}} [[Grave Room]]s ===
Grave Rooms are Rooms that appear in the {{s|Dark Room}} which only contain 1-3 [[Dirt Patch]]es. {{c|The Forgotten}} is unlocked by reaching this room and digging with {{i|Mom's Shovel}}.
{{slideshow
 | [[file:Dirt Patch.png]]
 | [[file:Dirt Patch Forgotten.png]]
}}

=== {{dlc+|r}} {{r|Mirror Room}} ===
[[File:Mirror_Door.png|98px]]

The Mirror Room is a single special room found on the second floor of Chapter 1.5, containing a single mirror on either the left or right doorway location. This mirror can be broken by explosions, but also can be entered to explore the [[Mirrored World]], a replica of the current floor, to find {{i|Knife Piece 1}}. The mirror can only be entered by {{C|The Lost}}, {{C|Tainted Lost}}, {{C|Tainted Forgotten}}, and {{C|Tainted Jacob}}'s ghost form. All other characters must touch the {{e|White Fire Place}} which always generates on the second floor of Chapter 1.5 in order to temporarily become The Lost in order to enter the mirror.{{dlc-}}

=== {{dlc+|r}} {{r|Mine Cart Room}} ===
{{slideshow
 | [[file:Mineshaft_Door_locked.png|98px]]
 | [[file:Mineshaft_Door_opened.png|98px]]
 | [[file:Mineshaft_Door_blocked.png|98px]]
}}

The Mine Cart Room is a single special room found on the second floor of Chapter 2.5 only if Isaac already has {{i|Knife Piece 1}}. It contains a Yellow Button, a single minecart, a blocked door at the top of the room and occasionally some enemies.

There are 2 other {{e|Yellow Button}}s located randomly on the same floor and pressing all 3 repairs the minecart's track allowing access through the blocked door. Alternatively having [[Flight]] and 2 bombs also allows access through the door. The area past the blocked door contains {{i| Knife Piece 2}} and a chase sequence with {{E|Mother's Shadow}}. The door is permanently blocked after leaving the sub-area.{{dlc-}}

== Notes ==
* In regular Rooms with unreachable enemies, the doors will automatically open after a while to prevent Isaac from becoming unable to progress. See [[User:Blcd/RandomTidbits#Room Anti-softlock|here]] for the specific details.
** This will not occur if Isaac has [[flight]] or if there is a boss or miniboss in the Room.
** This will not occur in Rooms with {{E|Pressure Plate}}s that do not have enemies or only have indestructible enemies such as {{E|Wall Hugger}}s or {{E|Stone Grimace}}s.
* Rooms that have obstacles in the middle covered by pits can often drop the room reward in the place of the destroyed obstacle. Because of that, it is advised avoiding touching that obstacle if you really need pickups.
* In short, the following types of special rooms no longer appear after a specific chapter, unless the player has collected specific items or trinkets:
** Treasure Rooms, Shops and Planetariums no longer appear from Chapter 4/4.5 onward
** Arcades and Vaults no longer appear from Chapter 5 onward
** Curse Rooms, Sacrifice Rooms, Challenge Rooms, and Boss Challenge Rooms no longer appear from Chapter 6 onward

